Yes, that's right, I'm thinking about making another race.  I fully expect
that no one will like the idea, just because new races are looked down upon
(apparently the current ones aren't differentiated enough?) But here it goes
anyway:  Automatons!  As in, human-like robots made of metal.  Being robots,
they would start off poison resistant.  They would also be unbreathing, and
uneating.  When I say uneating, I mean that they would neither get hungry,
nor would they be able to eat (I plan to modify the eat code to check if the
player is an automaton, and if so, prevent them from eating "You can't eat,
you have no digestive system!")  Maybe I should ban potions too ("You can't
drink!").  Or are potions magical, such that dumping them on a robot would
make them have their effect?.  Also, I'm considering preventing all
spellcasting, because these robot's aren't programmed such that they
understand magic (since all it takes to use a scroll is to read it aloud,
they could use scrolls).  It would possibly make them overpowered, but I
think they should also be immune to mind flayers (I mean, it's hard to
reason why a robot would lose it's memory when a purple tentacle attacks
it's head).  The final upshot would be, that being made of metal would make
them stoning resistant.  To balance this out, I'm wondering if I could make
it so that they would take extra damage from lightning based attacks.  Also,
although they can breathe under water, they aren't waterproof, so perhaps
I'll see about making it so that they take a damage while underwater, or
maybe even make it a delayed death ("You are slowing down."  "You are
rusting."  "Your joint's are grinding."  "You can't move."  You rust
completely.")

Maybe all this stuff is a little extreme, but I did really like the idea of
a completely foodless race, one that can't get intrinsics by eating, but
never goes hungry either.  And a race with no magic seemed interesting too.

As far as alignments, any would be possible (depends on the programmer), and
I'm not really sure about class restrictions.  Perhaps no valks, because
they are mythological warrior women, and somehow it doesn't seem that an
automaton would fit in.  I really think it would be interesting to have a
Automaton Wizard, perhaps that would be the "ultimate" challenge, a wizard
with no spells (or perhaps It'd be really dumb.  I know I'd never do it :))


